Z||000010||SLAMMED87GT||12-11-2001||02:54 PM||||Hey DR650- this may cheer you up somewhat knowing that your situation isn't as bad as mine was. <P>The first one: I was drving an '85 GT. This young *****  was driving way to close on a icy road. She was going to pass me and she drove very erattic to do so. She lost control of the car and slammed into the right rear quarter of my car. She was cited for reckless driving and later I found out that she had no insurance and I only had liability at the time.<P>The bill she was ordered to pay me: $3200<BR>I received a whopping $416 and no more. She left state and I haven't gotten anything else.<P>With my current ride, the 87GT:<P>I had to drive it the winter of '00 as I had no other car. One night I was parked down bu St.Cloud State University (lot of drunk kids driving around along with icy roads), I came out the next morning to find out someone had ran into my car, just so happens it was the about the same spot where my last Fiero was hit. Do you think they left a note on my windsheild with there phone number?  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> "hit and run"<P>Look at how my '87 GT used to look!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/'87crash1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/'87crash2.jpg"> <P>Total damage: $2300. <P>What did I do? I got if fixed and made my car even better than it was. I went to 19 shows this year and placed at many.<P>Sometimes you just got to stick your chest out and take it like a man. <P>BTW, I got pulled over today in the Beretta for no reason at all. The cops in my town are just bored.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||12-11-2001||03:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLAMMED87GT:<BR><B>Sometimes you just got to stick your chest out and take it like a man. <P>BTW, I got pulled over today in the Beretta for no reason at all. The cops in my town are just bored.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know the feeling.  I was having a bad day once (ok, I've had more than one, but I digress....) and this dude tells me to "Suck it up."  I was already p.o.'ed.  That just made me want to go postal.  But you're right.  Sometimes that's just what you gotta do.  And vent about it, too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So, what was the cop's reason for pulling your over?  Suspicious bumper stickers?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
