Z||000013||jelly2m8||12-11-2001||04:50 PM|||| Always sux when you have an accident, but How/ why did the cop charge you?  You said the roads were icy, its not like you were doing  over the posted speed limit and lost control of the car.<P>Around here the Police are not required if the damage looks to be less than 500 dollars. I can see buddy's point of calling them, even just fixing the dent and doing the paint work might cost that. Even then they usually just write up an accident report, they only give tickets if something obvious happened, ( on wrong side of road, not giving right away, drunk, etc).<P> But giving you a ticket? Dude, sounds like your getting the shaft here. I'd be seriously looking into that.<P> I also contact the guy you hit and ask him if he had an estimate done, maybe if it isn't too much money, he will let you pay for it out of your pocket. Might be cheaper in the long run to pay for the repairs, than have your insurance rates go over for the next 5 years or so.<P>good luck<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
